  "summary": "The South Pasadena City Council voted not to renew one of its two Flock Safety contracts, ending the use of 14 cameras, amid privacy concerns following reports that Southern California agencies illegally shared ALPR data with federal immigration authorities. The city shares data with Riverside County Sheriff's Office, one of the implicated agencies. Council also discussed shortening data retention from 30 to 15 days.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The South Pasadena City Council moved Wednesday not to renew a contract with Flock Safety",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "The council's decision follows public outcry after reports that some local law enforcement agencies in Southern California illegally shared license plate reader data with federal immigration agents.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "Many of our residents are very concerned about the misuse and abuse of data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 19
    },
    {
      "quote": "Council members also discussed shortening the time period that the city holds onto its data from 30 to 15 days.",
      "paragraph_idx": 22
    }
